  "2026-10-28T18:53:27.159Z",codex-agent,"CI compatibility repair completed without deleting or weakening existing assertions: the five failed native/source compatibility cases pass 5/5; linked adversarial tests pass 8/8; final interrupted-read, coherent-witness and completed-prefix checks pass 3/3, including unfinished non-read prefixes. Disposable legacy scripts pass 20/20 evidence and 10/10 reconciliation mutations. Fresh selected witness and history proofs each pass fixed, fail reverted by assertion and pass restored (2/2), in addition to the six original round-2 selected proofs. The replay read-only legacy contract is preserved; native inference still authenticates every pending hold/prompt. Missing observations are reconstructed solely through the read producer on unfinished proof copies, while completed proofs never fill gaps. Source-contract refusal precedence is preserved. Reuse completion now occurs in its supported branch instead of a redundant trailing pending-phase check. Typecheck, lint, build, zero duplication and all 167 declaration docstrings pass. Fresh full gates and complete branch coverage remain unverified on the forthcoming head; the last completed integration run remains 478/485 and 99.78 percent branches, and must not count as approval. Replacement run links will be maintained on PR 39 at the unchanged 18:59 UTC cutoff. No local test processes remain."
