  "2026-10-28T19:29:08.148Z",codex-agent,"Round 3 reproduction and focused evidence: the identity attack reproduced exactly, with three native children charging 23853 against a 20000 cap while the controller reported 7951. Clearing an intent independently erased 7951 from the receipt. The fix retains one native child and reports 7951 after repeated replacements; clearing a saved intent restores its native charge. Both new tests pass, all three component roles plus SDK case aliases pass, and the existing replay/legacy/placeholder focus passes 5/5. The full targeted refusal corpus passes 21/21. The prior-head CI actually completed 462/485 with 23 ordinary-replay/refusal failures, which all fall under the shared-verifier class; no old failure is being called approval. Typed refusal remedies, deterministic child identity, current SDK reads and native history now protect replay and repair recovery. Both the original 500-sequence journal model and a new independent 500-sequence identity/import model are running. Packed tests retain the original four partial/zero-remaining assertions and add identity replacement, cleared-intent and ordinary-refusal cases across every existing host."
  "2026-10-28T21:00:15.523Z",codex-agent,"Round 3 closes two classes: every replay validates execution refusals through the execution verifier; durable budget authority binds canonical child identity and native publisher history, including cleared intents and older native-state imports. Package-wide audit covered SDK replay/resume, repair continuation, JSON/TOON and packed consumers. The replacement baseline created 3 children charging 23853 against 20000 while reporting 7951; fixed behavior keeps one child and 7951. Seeded identity model passed 500 sequences (173 replacements, 133 cleared older intents); original journal model passed 500 sequences with 235 older replays. Original replay, identity and cleared-intent behavioral reverts all passed fixed, failed reverted and passed restored. Native-state rollback regression reproduced before the additional publisher-history guard; fixed native resume and repair resume now refuse further inference while retaining supported components. All 22 restored-intent interleaving boundaries passed on a real non-git tracker. Additional focused native-history, packed consumer and exact-head CI validation is in progress."
  "2026-10-28T21:04:24.973Z",codex-agent,"Public read-only validation rerun passed on the same pinned public corpus: 12 items, 54941 JSON bytes and all 30 files unchanged; runtime has no Git executable. One missing part among ten scheduled one logical child, reused nine components and supported ten, with two deterministic protocol requests and 8181 charged tokens. Resume added zero requests. Zero budget retained nine supported answers and one named gap; compact JSON is 2918 bytes. No external inference or provider billing claim. Typecheck, lint, zero-duplication gate, complete docstrings and build passed. Re-fetched main: zero commits behind. Untracked-allocation regression passed for both native repair children and unrelated foreign runs."
  "2026-10-28T21:26:55.773Z",codex-agent,"Round 3 behavioral revert proof is complete for eight focused cases: ordinary replay refusal validation, canonical child identities, cleared intents, native publisher-history authority, untracked native allocations, native usage counters, prior question contracts, and pending prompt authentication. Each fixed implementation passed; removing only the corresponding guard failed by assertion in a disposable copy; restoration passed again. Identity refusal persistence additionally proves repeated SDK/CLI resumes retain the named gap. The existing prompt and counter tests now call the verifier directly so publisher-history checks cannot mask their regressions. Native interchange property passed all 500 sequences through SDK read-back, covering eight source revisions, 246 older-input replays, 179 native-v1 and 321 native-v2 inputs; the publisher export equaled SDK state on every sequence. The linked publisher-history must-allow/must-refuse test passed through pm test (1/1), alongside the earlier linked recovery suite (5/5)."
