  "2026-10-28T22:03:53.923Z",codex-agent,"Merged main at 5c96b92 in bfb2637 and installed the approved 2026.10.25 toolchain. Its new large-legacy migration fixture initially omitted the native ownership fields that every package producer writes, so the existing stale/foreign-write fence correctly refused its save. The fixture now supplies its original parent, rlm:call marker and rlm_run identity; all original read, historical-read, save, GC and equality assertions remain unchanged. The production ownership fence is retained. This corrects fixture provenance without granting inline foreign JSON write authority. Explicit unbounded native reads also unwrap the SDK's typed read envelope through the same SDK-record boundary used by main's ledger fix. Merged-SDK focused tests, the new large-intent behavioral revert, static checks and public measurement are running."
  "2026-10-28T22:07:42.139Z",codex-agent,"Merged-SDK focused checks passed 4/4, including the reported 20000-token identity attack (one native child, 7951 charged), ordinary refusal replay, large legacy historical reads and large repair intents. The extra description-budget hypothesis was disproved: reverting its unbounded flags still passed the large-intent case, because this SDK's normal core-description read is already complete. I reverted those unnecessary description-consumer changes and their newly added invalid proof, while retaining the large-intent must-allow test and every original test/assertion. Only main's proven large-custom-field historical-read fix is required. The eight actual behavioral revert proofs remain unchanged and passed. Public validation on SDK 2026.10.25 also passed with exactly the original measurements: 12 items, 54941 bytes, 30 unchanged files, 1 scheduled child, 9 reused, 10 supported, 8181 tokens, no additional resume requests and 2918 compact bytes."
  "2026-10-28T22:14:15.225Z",codex-agent,"Final local integration evidence: merged-SDK focused suite 4/4; linked large-intent must-allow test passed through pm test 1/1 on SDK 2026.10.25; typecheck, lint, zero-duplication gate, complete docstrings and build passed; strict health authority is ok with existing advisory warnings. Public non-git read-only validation reproduced all measured numbers without changing source files. Earlier compatibility evidence is retained with its version boundary: authentication 8/8, global npm/Bun packed acceptance 2/2 with eight receipts each, three seeded models of at least 500 sequences, eight genuine fixed/reverted/restored proofs, and 22 restored-intent interleaving boundaries. All supplied round-3 findings are fixed; prior prompt/hold/reuse regressions remain. No original test or assertion was weakened or deleted. The extra core-description budget hypothesis was disproved and its unnecessary changes reverted. Exact pushed-head full npm and Bun release gates remain required; run URLs, counts and any pending state will be reported on PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/pull/39 within the 30-minute CI wait limit. Item remains in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-28T22:23:52.201Z",codex-agent,"Final independent-verifier audit is complete. Added direct SDK assertions to the existing unreachable-call and oversized settled-usage regressions so publisher-history protection cannot mask either verifier. No original assertion was removed. The unreachable-call behavioral revert passed fixed, failed on guard removal, then passed restored on SDK 2026.10.25; the settled-usage case passed 1/1. There are now nine genuine focused revert cases across the documented SDK pins. Fresh typecheck, lint and zero duplication passed. Reclaimed only for this final validation work and releasing again now. All round-3 blockers and prior supplied findings are fixed; final full npm/Bun release-gate evidence remains pending on the exact pushed head and will be recorded in PR 39 with run URLs and counts. No new SDK gap was found."
  "2026-10-28T22:55:10.021Z",codex-agent,"Exact-head CI 40779877829 at c6b258f failed the Node 26 coverage gate: 496/500 tests passed; four failures were three behavioral-revert subtests and their parent. Coverage was statements/functions/lines 100, branches 99.64. The three harness issues are corrected: direct prefix verifier assertions prevent prompt/history fences masking remedy checks; the read-lock mutant avoids artificial reentrant storage deadlock during fixture setup; stale by-value and ambiguous aggregate-version snippets now match their intended functions. Focused component-remedy test passed 1/1 and fresh typecheck/lint/zero duplication passed. No original assertion or coverage threshold was weakened. Full harness verification remains pending, and branch-coverage gaps in engine, ledger and repair remain unresolved. The PR is being marked draft because the full-gate acceptance is unmet. A fresh exact-head CI run will be linked on PR 39; the original 30-minute wait cutoff remains unchanged. Claim released; item remains in progress for continuation."
  "2026-10-28T23:57:00.662Z",codex-agent,"Resumed on exact head bb7aa2d4 for the new parse-refusal failure and branch coverage. The shared verifier currently catches parseAction errors and continues without authenticating the recorded refusal, while ordinary replay and resume have separate recordedAction checks. This violates one-verifier agreement and lets direct validation used by repair skip refusal fields. Plan: route verification through the existing parser/refusal producer check, audit all code/reason/remedy fields with seeded adversarial cases, preserve legacy must-allow records, add behavior-revert evidence, and close the uncovered real state branches without changing thresholds. Main has zero commits ahead; SDK pin stays 2026.10.25. The new instruction allows a 45-minute exact-head CI wait."
  "2026-10-29T00:37:25.874Z",codex-agent,"The exact-head failure reproduced locally (0/1). Code fix routes shared validation through recordedAction instead of swallowing parse errors; replay, resume and repair now share that refusal authentication, while a final unobserved producer response may still resume before its parse decision is recorded. The seeded property additionally found child reconstruction could overwrite a saved code with evidence when a remedy existed. One recordedRefusal contract now validates child/hook metadata in both SDK hydration and reconstruction. Property passed 500 mutations over eight SDK-produced refusal records and 24 field positions; SDK read-back then proved replay/resume/repair reject each field mutation with no inference or item/history writes. Both new behavioral reversions passed fixed, failed by assertion on the reverted code, and passed restored (2/2). No existing assertion or threshold is weakened. New edge fixtures cover legacy held usage, malformed births, immutable payload corruption, native component declarations, unfinished parse responses and graph completeness. A repeated-spawn probe also exposed materialization before the inference fence; spawn now refuses untrusted progress before any native mutation, and the test checks unchanged SDK item state."
  "2026-10-29T00:47:47.953Z",codex-agent,"Round 4 validation: the exact failing bb7aa2d parse-remedy case reproduces 0/1 and now passes 1/1, including a linked pm test run. Focused shared refusal/recovery suite passes 11/11 (500 seeded mutations, eight SDK producer records, 24 independently authenticated field positions); native authority selection passes 3/3. Behavioral proof removes each new verifier guard independently: fixed pass, reverted assertion failure, restored pass (2/2). Rule: every persisted refusal must be checked against its producer contract before replay or inference, including parse failures and terminal child/hook receipts. Audited SDK, CLI JSON/TOON and packed consumers through their common verifier. Branch probes exercise legacy held usage, damaged publisher payloads, canonical births, component contracts, genuine interrupted responses, ordinary graph completeness and stripped declarations. Typecheck, lint, build, docstrings and zero-duplication pass. Original coverage thresholds remain 100/100/100/100; complete npm and Bun release evidence will be taken from fresh exact-head CI. The PR remains draft until green."
  "2026-10-29T01:14:33.577Z",codex-agent,"Exact-head CI ddf11da reports 506/511 and 99.89% branches. A supposedly redundant ordinary spawn check also authenticated absent observations, so removing it changed interrupted replay behavior; the common verifier now performs that check in observational mode. Existing recovery and malformed-observation assertions remain unchanged. Two older source-revert scripts still pointed at the former duplicate parse validation and parser-call count; their mutation targets now follow the shared verifier, retaining every behavioral assertion. Additional branch fixtures cover unversioned full-slice partitions, missing earlier proof reads and untracked allocations with an unmaterialized target. The first-push 45-minute verification cutoff remains unchanged. Both CI run links and subsequent results are recorded on PR 39."
  "2026-10-29T01:17:41.683Z",codex-agent,"CI scheduling: every supported Node version retains one complete unchanged coverage/release gate, with the npm wrapper on Node 22 and Bun wrapper on Node 26. Manual verification now invokes those two full release wrappers in parallel instead of running three sequential full suites on Node 26. PR checks retain the complete npm gate steps on Node 22 and the complete Bun release gate on Node 26. No test, release command, source inventory or 100-percent threshold is removed. This avoids duplicate coverage work inside the fixed first-push verification window."
  "2026-10-29T01:21:29.774Z",codex-agent,"Follow-up focused evidence: interrupted recovery, malformed spawn observations, unversioned full-slice partition receipts and untracked allocations pass 4/4; the added saved-legacy-parser fixture passes independently 1/1 with its exact invalid/Unknown model action refusal. All five updated round-three behavioral reverts pass by assertion with source restored byte-for-byte, including both resume and replay routing through the shared verifier. Follow-up typecheck, lint, duplication, docstrings, build and changelog check pass. The original 20 evidence reverts and the two new 500-mutation verifier reverts also passed. No existing assertion or coverage threshold was weakened."
  "2026-10-29T01:25:34.063Z",codex-agent,"Packed follow-up: the newly added parse regression initially passed a differently named inference-blocking model to resume, so the supported model-identity precondition correctly refused before receipt authentication. The fixture now retains the exact saved model name while keeping its RlmTranscriptError/remedy and zero-extra-inference assertions unchanged. Existing packed acceptance assertions are untouched. Updated constrained behavioral reverts also pass 8/8; the round-three routing reverts pass 5/5. Original 45-minute cutoff remains fixed."
